Two sides of a triangle are $10\text{ cm}$ and $15\text{ cm}$, with an included angle of $60^{\circ}$. Choose an appropriate rule and find the third side $x$, correct to one decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (C) at (1.5,2.598);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$15\text{ cm}$};\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$10\text{ cm}$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\pic[draw,"$60^{\circ}$",angle radius=7mm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

